course: dictionary
lesson: 12611
title: Discredited: not to be believed
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Discredited means shown to be false, or no longer believed. It can also mean that people have lost their trust or respect for someone. The word comes from discredit, and the prefix dis- makes it mean the opposite of believing.
explain: «Scientists found new evidence, so the old theory was discredited.» The new evidence showed the theory was wrong, so people stopped believing it. Discredited here means shown to be false.
explain: «After the lies came out, the mayor was discredited.» The lies made people lose their trust in the mayor. Discredited here means that people no longer respect him. Always check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: "shown to be false" or "no longer trusted" should make sense.
fact: Discredited means shown to be false, or not to be believed.
fact: «A discredited theory» is an idea that evidence has shown to be wrong.
fact: A person can be discredited when lies or scandals make people lose their trust or respect.
fact: Discredit is a verb, so discredited is its past form: «The report was discredited.»
fact: When a word is discredited, the reader should not trust it.
exercise: «The scientist's idea was discredited when new evidence proved it wrong.» What does discredited mean here? | Made into a film | Shown to be famous | *Shown to be false | Painted in bright colours
exercise: Jo says, «The newspaper was discredited after it printed lies.» What does discredited suggest? | *Readers stopped trusting it | It was sold in every shop | Readers loved it even more | It became bigger and better
exercise: Find and copy the one word that means not believed. «The discredited theory was taught for years, but the evidence showed it was wrong.» | theory | taught | years | *discredited
test: «After the lies came out, the mayor was discredited.» What does this tell you? | People love the mayor more than ever | *People no longer trust the mayor | The mayor moved to a new house | The mayor won a prize for honesty
test: Which sentence shows an idea that has been discredited? | The idea was drawn in a big book. | The idea was tested and became famous. | *The evidence proved the idea wrong, so nobody believes it now. | Everyone chose the idea for a school project.
exam: «The fake report was discredited by the experts.» Which word is closest in meaning to discredited? | Celebrated | *Disproved | Copied | Believed
